ay that the transaction is unlikely to restrict competition because TPG’s activities in private equity and infant and toddler nutrition…","Lotte Group agreed on Aug."],"body":"MLex Summary: TPG, a US private-equity firm based in Fort Worth, Texas, has secured unconditional approval from South Korea’s antitrust regulator to acquire Lotte Rental through affiliate Lexicon Korea Holdco. The Korea Fair Trade Commission said Tuesday that the transaction is unlikely to restrict competition because TPG’s activities in private equity and infant and toddler nutrition products are unrelated to Lotte Rental’s domestic vehicle-rental business. Lotte Group agreed on Aug. 11 to sell the entire 61.2 percent stake in Lotte Rental held by Hotel Lotte and Busan Lotte Hotel to TPG for about 1.3 trillion won ($946.7 million). The sale follows an earlier attempt to sell Lotte Rental to Affinity Equity Partners, which the regulator blocked in January over concerns that the deal would restrict competition.\n\nMLex identifies risk to business wherever it emerges, with specialist reporters across the globe providing exclusive news and deep-dive analysis on the proposals, probes, enforcement actions and rulings that matter to your organization and clients, now and in the longer term.\n\nExperience MLex today with a 14-day free trial.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: A verification email will be sent to your address before you can access your trial.\n\nCountry Afghanistan Albania Algeria American Samoa Andorra Angola Anguilla Antarctica Antigua and Barbuda Argentina Armenia Aruba Australia Austria Azerbaijan Bahamas Bahrain Bangladesh Barbados Belarus Belgium Belize Benin Bermuda Bhutan Bolivia Bosnia Botswana Bouvet Island Brazil British Indian Ocean Territory British Virgin Islands Brunei Bulgaria Burkina Faso Burundi Cambodia Cameroon Canada Cape Verde Caribbean Netherlands Cayman Islands Central African Republic Chad Chile China Christmas Island Cocos (Keeling) Islands Colombia Comoros Congo - Brazzaville 